## ✅ PART 1: Train Naive Bayes Model in Python

### 1.1 Install requirements

```bash
pip install scikit-learn pandas nltk
```

### 1.2 Python Code to Train and Export Model

```python
# train_sarcasm_model.py

import pandas as pd
import json
from sklearn.feature_extraction.text import CountVectorizer
from sklearn.naive_bayes import MultinomialNB

# 1. Sample dataset (you can expand it)
data = {
    "text": [
        "Yeah right, that was amazing",       # Sarcastic
        "I love spending time in traffic",    # Sarcastic
        "What a surprise, he failed again",   # Sarcastic
        "I had a great day at the park",      # Not Sarcastic
        "She is really talented",             # Not Sarcastic
        "The food was delicious",             # Not Sarcastic
    ],
    "label": [1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0]  # 1 = Sarcastic, 0 = Not
}

df = pd.DataFrame(data)

# 2. Vectorize text
vectorizer = CountVectorizer(binary=True)
X = vectorizer.fit_transform(df["text"])
y = df["label"]

# 3. Train Naive Bayes model
model = MultinomialNB()
model.fit(X, y)

# 4. Export vocabulary and class log probabilities
export_data = {
    "vocabulary": vectorizer.vocabulary_,
    "class_log_prior": model.class_log_prior_.tolist(),
    "feature_log_prob": model.feature_log_prob_.tolist(),
    "classes": model.classes_.tolist()
}

# 5. Save to JSON
with open("naive_bayes_model.json", "w") as f:
    json.dump(export_data, f)

print("Model exported to naive_bayes_model.json")
```

